      "description": "Watch Czech Republic vs Croatia highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 26, 2026. The UEFA Nations League stage was set for a compelling showdown as the Czech Republic hosted Croatia on September 26, 2026 . Both nations entered the contest seeking to assert their dominance in a fixture known for its tactical intrigue and technical quality. Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Half The first half was characterized by disciplined defending and a cautious approach from both sides. Croatia attempted to break the deadlock through set-pieces, with Ivan Perišić and Luka Sučić delivering dangerous crosses that failed to find a clinical finish. Igor Matanović had a notable opportunity with a header that went wide, while the Czech Republic focused on maintaining their shape. The tension was evident when Lukáš Červ was shown a yellow card for a robust challenge, but despite the intensity, neither side could find the back of the net before the interval. A Rapid Exchange of Goals The match exploded into life immediately after the restart. In the 47th minute, the legendary Luka Modrić gave Croatia the lead with a right-footed strike that took a deflection past the goalkeeper following a setup by Matanović . The hosts, however, refused to be cowed and leveled the scores just seven minutes later. Adam Karabec capitalized on a defensive lapse by Luka Vušković to fire home with his left foot, rewarding the Czech persistence after an assist from Adam Hložek . VAR Heartbreak and Pašalić’s Decisive Header As the clock ticked down, the game swung back in favor of the visitors. In the 77th minute, Marco Pašalić rose highest to meet a cross from Ivan Perišić , powering a header into the net to restore the Croatian advantage. Drama ensued shortly after when the Czech Republic thought they had equalized again, only for VAR to intervene and rule the goal out for offside. Despite late pressure and a yellow card for Vladimír Coufal for dissent, Croatia held firm. A crucial late save by Lukáš Horníček from Ante Budimir kept the margin thin, but Croatia ultimately secured the victory in a thrilling encounter."
